The methods in interfaces are abstracts, but we can use a magic word named "default" there we can implement the method
thus we dont have to override the method in classes that implement the method.
In this case is like a method in the super class of inheriting class. But before we think they are the same thing, halt.
The use of this word is for future updates to existing interfaces, assume we have an interface that we need to update
we can simply add a default word method and it will update all the implementing classes instead of updating each class
individually so this will be backward compatible.

We can also overload existing methods in case we want to add a default method.
